    "text": "Aillén Trechenn was a triple-headed monster of Irish myth. He attacked Ireland's great capital, Tara, and the regional capital of Emain Macha in Ulster. Writers describe him sometimes as male and sometimes as female. The monster lived in the cave called Oweynagat at the Connacht capital of Cruachan. The poet Amairgin finally dispatched the monster and freed Tara from its grip. Because the usual resident of Oweynagat is the Mórrígan, this figure may be connected with her. The difference between this murderous monster and Aillén mac Midgna is hard to tell.",
